The lepton decay ratios in $b\to s\ell^+\ell^-$ transitions exhibit significant tension with the Standard Model. This study demonstrates that the semi-inclusive decay lepton decay ratios maintain equality, even accounting for finite $\ell$-mass effects. Consequently, the observed divergence in the decay ratios $R_{e/\mu}$ and $R_{e/\mu}^{\mathrm{ab}}$ cannot stem from the final lepton decay channels. Furthermore, the study investigates the impact of finite $\ell$-mass effects on the relevant decay and decay-lepton variables. Additionally, the semi-inclusive lepton decay functions $J_1$ and $J_2$ are derived for the first time. In the massless limit, these functions align with the full mass-dependent results. The numerical analysis indicates that the semi-inclusive lepton decay functions $J_1$ and $J_2$ exhibit a smooth behavior across the kinematic region of interest. The primary findings of this work are summarized as follows:
\begin{itemize}
    \item The semi-inclusive lepton decay functions in $b\to s\ell^+\ell^-$ transitions are derived for the first time.
    \item The finite $\ell$-mass effects on the semi-inclusive lepton decay functions are examined.
    \item The lepton decay functions in the semi-inclusive $b\to s\ell^+\ell^-$ transition exhibit the same behavior as the full decay functions.
    \item The lepton decay functions in the semi-inclusive $b\to s\ell^+\ell^-$ transition are found to be independent of the final lepton decay channel.
\end{itemize}
These results demonstrate that the semi-inclusive lepton decay functions in $b\to s\ell^+\ell^-$ transitions are robust against final-state lepton mass effects. The study also derives semi-inclusive lepton decay functions for the $b\to c\ell^+\ell^-$ transition. The primary conclusions are:
\begin{itemize}
    \item The semi-inclusive lepton decay functions in $b\to c\ell^+\ell^-$ transitions are derived.
    \item The lepton decay functions in the semi-inclusive $b\to c\ell^+\ell^-$ transition are found to be mutually independent.
\end{itemize}
